{"ts": 0.27703, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97m✓ Stage 4 cleared.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nYou can now:\r\n  \u001b[92mcommand -v    \u001b[0m \u001b[90mis this program installed?\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mwc            \u001b[0m \u001b[90mcount lines and words\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mseq           \u001b[0m \u001b[90mcount out numbers\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mhead          \u001b[0m \u001b[90mshow the first lines only\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92msort          \u001b[0m \u001b[90mput lines in order\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mgrep          \u001b[0m \u001b[90mkeep the lines that match\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92m|             \u001b[0m \u001b[90mfeed one output into the next command\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92m>  >>  <  *   \u001b[0m \u001b[90mto a file, add, from a file, match many\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[90mNext: Stage 5 · Ready for vimtutor\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m for Stage 5, or \u001b[92mquit\u001b[93m to stop here. Your place is saved.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 703}
{"ts": 0.277434, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 251}
